From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: fail buffer allocations that do not fit with
 -ENOMEM

A CAPTURE buffer of a 6144x3456 10-bit H.265 picture in P010 takes
111 MB with its reference surface, so a pool of seven or eight of them
does not fit on a 1 GB board. The allocation does not fail, though:
vb2-dma-contig allocates with GFP_KERNEL through the IOMMU DMA
allocator, whose final order-0 page allocations may invoke the OOM
killer. The decoding process maps none of these buffers (they are
exported as dma-bufs), so the victim is another process: the desktop
shell or the login shell, while the decoder carries on allocating.

Allocate the buffers of both queues and the H.265 per-buffer motion
vector buffers with __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL: the page allocator reclaims as
hard as before, then fails the allocation instead of killing a process,
and VIDIOC_REQBUFS/VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS (or the decode job) return
-ENOMEM, which userspace can act on. The flag reaches the page
allocator unchanged: vb2_dc_alloc_coherent() passes
GFP_KERNEL | q->gfp_flags to dma_alloc_attrs(), and
__iommu_dma_alloc_pages() adds only __GFP_NOWARN, __GFP_HIGHMEM and,
for the optional higher orders, __GFP_NORETRY.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c  | 3 ++-
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
index bd5563ac6..9cca1007a 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
@@ -465,7 +465,8 @@ static int cedrus_h265_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 			dma_alloc_attrs(dev->dev,
 					cedrus_buf->codec.h265.mv_col_buf_size,
 					&cedrus_buf->codec.h265.mv_col_buf_dma,
-					GFP_KERNEL, DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING);
+					GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL,
+					DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING);
 		if (!cedrus_buf->codec.h265.mv_col_buf) {
 			cedrus_buf->codec.h265.mv_col_buf_size = 0;
 			return -ENOMEM;
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index c54adf35d..7363d1e26 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -1001,6 +1001,13 @@ int cedrus_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq,
 	src_vq->lock = &ctx->dev->dev_mutex;
 	src_vq->dev = ctx->dev->dev;
 	src_vq->supports_requests = true;
+	/*
+	 * Fail an allocation that does not fit with -ENOMEM instead of
+	 * invoking the OOM killer: a 6K 10-bit CAPTURE buffer takes over
+	 * 100 MB, and the decoder's own process, whose buffers are not mapped,
+	 * would not be the one killed.
+	 */
+	src_vq->gfp_flags = __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL;
 	src_vq->requires_requests = true;
 
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(src_vq);
@@ -1017,6 +1024,7 @@ int cedrus_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq,
 	dst_vq->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_COPY;
 	dst_vq->lock = &ctx->dev->dev_mutex;
 	dst_vq->dev = ctx->dev->dev;
+	dst_vq->gfp_flags = __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL;
 
 	return vb2_queue_init(dst_vq);
 }
-- 
